  586,
  'sindh-government-graduate-internship-program-2026',
  'Sindh Government Graduate Internship Program 2026 – Registration, Eligibility & Updates',
  'internships',
  'Government of Sindh (Information & Youth Affairs / I Work for Sindh)',
  'Internship (Provincial Government)',
  'Sindh, Pakistan (All Districts: Karachi, Hyderabad, Sukkur, Larkana, Mirpurkhas, Shaheed Benazirabad)',
  'Bachelor''s / Master''s Degree (14 to 16+ Years Education from HEC-Recognized University)',
  'Monthly Stipend (To Be Confirmed by Government of Sindh Notification)',
  'Expected November 2026 (Announcement Phase)',
  '2026-11-07',
  'https://iwork4sindh.gos.pk',
  'https://iwork4sindh.gos.pk',
  1,
  'SINDH',
  '/images/sindh-government-graduate-internship-program-2026.webp',
  'Sindh Government Graduate Internship Program 2026 Official Registration Eligibility Updates CareerDost Guide',
  'The Government of Sindh has announced a new Graduate Internship Program for fresh degree holders across the province. Check the latest status, expected eligibility criteria, registration timeline on the I Work for Sindh portal, and official updates.',
  '["# Sindh Government Graduate Internship Program 2026 – Registration, Eligibility & Updates","## Executive Summary & Official Provincial Announcement\n\nThe **Government of Sindh** has officially announced the upcoming launch of a comprehensive **Graduate Internship Program 2026** targeted at fresh university graduates across all administrative divisions of Sindh.\n\nThe high-level announcement was made on **29 October 2026** by Sindh Senior Minister Sharjeel Inam Memon during a media briefing in Karachi. The initiative is conceived as a multi-sector bridge designed to connect educated youth with structured practical workplace experience, addressing the critical employment gap confronting recent university pass-outs in Karachi, Hyderabad, Sukkur, Larkana, Mirpurkhas, Shaheed Benazirabad, and rural Sindh.\n\nWhile the provincial leadership has signaled that operational rollout is targeted for **November 2026**, formal administrative notifications covering quotas, monthly stipends, department allocations, and portal registration modules are currently in final departmental clearance.","> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Official Announcement Status & Verification Notice:**\n> Registration details and the official application procedure have not yet been confirmed. Candidates should wait for the official Government of Sindh announcement. Do not submit sensitive personal documents or pay processing charges to unverified websites, third-party portals, or unauthorized WhatsApp groups.","## Program Overview & Key Details\n\n| Parameter | Official Details |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Sponsoring Authority** | Government of Sindh (Youth & Information Initiatives) |\n| **Program Title** | Sindh Government Graduate Internship Program 2026 |\n| **Recruitment Category** | Public Sector Graduate Internship (Provincial) |\n| **Target Beneficiaries** | Fresh University Degree Holders (Bachelors / Masters) |\n| **Targeted Launch Month** | November 2026 (Announcement Phase) |\n| **Official Digital Portal** | I Work for Sindh ([iwork4sindh.gos.pk](https://iwork4sindh.gos.pk)) |\n| **Current Registration Status** | Awaiting Official Gazette Notification & Portal Activation |\n| **Geographic Scope** | All 30 Districts of Sindh (Urban & Rural) |\n| **Stipend Status** | Under Provincial Cabinet Review (Official Figure Awaited) |\n| **Application Mode** | Online (Once Portal Formally Activated) |\n| **Application Fee** | Rs. 0 (Free of Cost for Verified Provincial Initiatives) |","## What is the Sindh Graduate Internship Program?\n\nThe Sindh Graduate Internship Program represents a proactive youth empowerment policy designed to address youth underemployment across Sindh. In recent years, thousands of qualified graduates from universities in Sindh have struggled to secure initial professional footholds due to private and public employers requiring prior hands-on work history.\n\nKey pillars highlighted in the provincial announcement include:\n\n- **Structured Workplace Exposure:** Placements are planned across provincial ministries, autonomous public bodies, educational institutions, development authorities, and affiliated corporate partners.\n- **Market-Driven Skill Integration:** Alongside regular administrative and technical duties, the Sindh Government intends to integrate specialized short training modules focused on high-demand technical and managerial skill sets.\n- **Mentorship & Evaluation:** Participating host institutions will be tasked with providing designated mentors to evaluate intern performance, culminating in an official Sindh Government Experience Certificate upon successful completion.","## Expected Target Audience & Candidate Eligibility (Announcement-Based)\n\nBecause the formal gazette notification has not yet been promulgated by the Sindh Services, General Administration & Coordination Department (SGA&CD), eligibility criteria remain **announcement-based and indicative**. Based on established Sindh government graduate protocols, candidates can expect the following benchmarks:\n\n1. **Educational Qualification:**\n   - Minimum 14 to 16 years of completed formal education (Graduation: BS, BA (Hons), B.Com, BBA, BE, MBBS, PharmD, or Master''s degrees: MA, MSc, MBA, MS).\n   - Degrees must be issued by a university chartered and recognized by the Higher Education Commission (HEC) of Pakistan.\n   - Indicative priority disciplines include Information Technology, Computer Science, Engineering, Management Sciences, Social Sciences, Commerce, and Agriculture.\n2. **Provincial Domicile Requirement:**\n   - Candidates must hold a verifiable **Domicile** and **Permanent Residence Certificate (PRC / Form D)** from any district of Sindh.\n   - Quotas are expected to balance representation between Urban Sindh (Karachi, Hyderabad, Sukkur) and Rural Sindh districts.\n3. **Graduation Cut-Off & Age Bracket:**\n   - Typically, government graduate internship initiatives restrict eligibility to fresh pass-outs who have completed their degrees within the preceding 2 to 3 years.\n   - Upper age ceilings for provincial graduate internships generally range between 28 and 30 years, subject to standard provincial age relaxation rules.","> [!TIP]\n> Candidates awaiting final semester result declarations or thesis clearances should actively request their provisional certificates or transcripts from their respective universities (such as University of Karachi, NED UET, MUET Jamshoro, University of Sindh, or IBA Karachi) to be fully prepared when registration opens.","## Registration Status & How to Apply Once Portal Opens\n\nAt present, **online registration is NOT active**. The Government of Sindh is preparing the digital infrastructure on the **I Work for Sindh** portal ([iwork4sindh.gos.pk](https://iwork4sindh.gos.pk)) and official Information Department channels.\n\nOnce the official recruitment circular is gazetted, the anticipated step-by-step registration procedure will operate as follows:\n\n1. **Official Portal Access:** Navigate exclusively to [iwork4sindh.gos.pk](https://iwork4sindh.gos.pk) or the designated portal announced on the Sindh Government Information Department website ([sindhinformation.gos.pk](https://sindhinformation.gos.pk)).\n2. **CNIC Registration:** Create a verified candidate profile by entering your 13-digit Computerized National Identity Card (CNIC) number, active mobile contact, and email address.\n3. **Profile Completion:** Enter academic scores, degree titles, graduating year, institutional details, and select your home district from the Sindh domicile dropdown.\n4. **Document Scans:** Upload clean, high-resolution PDF or JPEG scans of your educational degree/provisional certificate, CNIC (front and back), Form-D PRC, and recent passport-size photograph.\n5. **Preference Selection:** Select preferred placement fields (e.g., Administration, IT & Digital Services, Education, Finance, Public Infrastructure).\n6. **Submission & Tracking:** Submit the application without paying any fee and retain your digital submission tracking code for merit list tracking.","## Documents Candidates May Need (Commonly Required Civil Records)\n\nTo ensure swift submission when the application window goes live, applicants are strongly advised to keep the following standard verification documents in order. Please note that these items reflect standard civil service requirements and are subject to the final published rules:\n\n- **Valid CNIC / Smart Card** issued by NADRA showing an address in Sindh.\n- **Sindh Domicile Certificate** issued by the relevant Deputy Commissioner''s Office.\n- **Form D / Permanent Residence Certificate (PRC)** verifying provincial belonging.\n- **Higher Education Commission (HEC) Recognized Degree / Transcript** from your university.\n- **Provisional Result Card / Passing Certificate** if the formal convocation degree has not yet been issued.\n- **Passport-Sized Photographs** (white or blue background, recent).\n- **Disability Certificate** (if applying under the provincial 5% disabled quota, issued by the Sindh Social Welfare Department).\n\nFor a full breakdown of civil verification guidelines, consult our detailed [Government Jobs Documents Checklist for Pakistan 2026](/jobs/government-jobs-documents-checklist-pakistan-2026).","## Critical Scam Warning & Official Update Channels\n\nWhenever a high-profile provincial youth program is announced, fraudulent online pages, scam job portals, and unverified social media channels attempt to deceive job seekers. Maintain vigilance by adhering to these safety guidelines:\n\n- **Zero Registration Fee:** Legitimate government internship initiatives funded by the Sindh public treasury do not charge registration, processing, or challan fees. If a site demands payment via Easypaisa, JazzCash, or bank transfer to register, it is fraudulent.\n- **No Third-Party Google Forms:** The Government of Sindh will never accept official internship applications through informal Google Forms or unverified Facebook groups.\n- **Official Verification Only:** Bookmark the official Sindh Information Department portal ([sindhinformation.gos.pk](https://sindhinformation.gos.pk)) and CareerDost for vetted updates as soon as the gazette notification is issued.","## Related Sindh Career & Education Opportunities\n\nWhile awaiting the opening of the graduate internship portal, explore active provincial employment and skill pathways on CareerDost:\n\n- **Pillar Career Guide:** [Sindh Government Jobs 2026 — Latest Vacancies & Department Portal Guide](/jobs/sindh-government-jobs-2026)\n- **Provincial Internship Placement:** [SESSI Internship Programme 2026 — Karachi Openings](/jobs/sessi-internship-programme-2026)\n- **Clerical & Departmental Recruitment:** [Sindh Job Portal Guide — Junior Clerk Vacancies](/jobs/sindh-job-portal-2026-junior-clerk-jobs)\n- **Academic & Research Funding:** [Sindh HEC Research Grants 2026–27 (Up to Rs 5 Million)](/jobs/sindh-hec-research-support-programme-2026-27)\n- **Provincial Wage Standards:** [Sindh Minimum Wage 2026 — Workers Salary Baseline](/jobs/sindh-minimum-wage-2026-workers-salary)\n- **Women Mobility Scheme:** [Sindh Pink Scooty Scheme 2026 — Online Registration & Eligibility](/jobs/sindh-pink-scooty-scheme-2026-online-registration-eligibility)","## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\n\n### Q1: Is registration currently open for the Sindh Graduate Internship Program 2026?\n**No.** Online registration is not currently open. The Government of Sindh announced the framework on 29 October 2026, with portal deployment and formal notification targeted for November 2026. Stay tuned to CareerDost for real-time alerts.\n\n### Q2: What is the monthly stipend for the Sindh Graduate Internship Program?\nThe exact monthly stipend amount has not yet been confirmed by the Sindh Finance Department. Unofficial rumors circulating on social media regarding fixed stipend packages are unverified. CareerDost will publish the exact monetary figures once the official gazette notification is signed.\n\n### Q3: What is the official portal for the Sindh internship?\nThe program is scheduled to be managed through the official provincial workforce portal, **I Work for Sindh** at [iwork4sindh.gos.pk](https://iwork4sindh.gos.pk), coordinated with the Government of Sindh Information Department.\n\n### Q4: Can candidates with a domicile outside Sindh apply?\nNo. This initiative is an exclusively provincial program financed by the provincial exchequer for youth residing in Sindh. Applicants must possess a valid Sindh Domicile and PRC (Form-D).\n\n### Q5: What degree qualifications will be required?\nThe program is designated for graduate degree holders, meaning candidates possessing 14 to 16+ years of education (BS, BA, B.Com, BBA, BE, MA, MSc, or equivalent) from HEC-recognized higher education institutions.\n\n### Q6: How long will the internship last?\nThe official duration (whether 3 months, 6 months, or 12 months) is pending formal announcement in the program''s operational manual. Full parameters will be updated here immediately upon release.","## Official Links & Information Sources\n\n- **Provincial Workforce Portal:** [I Work for Sindh — iwork4sindh.gos.pk](https://iwork4sindh.gos.pk)\n- **Information Department, Sindh:** [Information & Archives Department — sindhinformation.gos.pk](https://sindhinformation.gos.pk)\n- **Government of Sindh Official Portal:** [Government of Sindh — sindh.gov.pk](https://sindh.gov.pk)\n\n*CareerDost is Pakistan''s independent career verification portal. All information in this announcement guide is verified against official government briefings and public service notifications.*"]',
  'Sindh Graduate Internship Program 2026: Status & Registration Guide',
  'Sindh Government Graduate Internship Program 2026 announced for degree holders. Check official status, expected eligibility, I Work for Sindh portal updates & FAQs.',
  'Sindh Government Graduate Internship Program 2026',
  'https://careerdost.blog/jobs/sindh-government-graduate-internship-program-2026',
  'Sindh Government Graduate Internship Program 2026 – Latest Official Updates',
  'Government of Sindh announces upcoming Graduate Internship Program for degree holders across Sindh. Full status overview, expected criteria, portal updates & scam warnings.',
  'published',
  'Fresh Graduates / Degree Holders',
  'Provincial Graduate Placements (TBA)',
  1,
  1,
  '2026-11-07T15:36:07.676Z',
  '2026-11-07T15:36:07.676Z'
);

