  1,
  'GATES',
  '/images/gates-cambridge-scholarship-2027.webp',
  'Gates Cambridge Scholarship 2027 University of Cambridge Fully Funded UK Postgraduate Scholarship CareerDost Guide',
  'The Gates Cambridge Scholarship 2027 offers fully funded postgraduate study (MPhil, MLitt, PhD) at the University of Cambridge for outstanding international applicants, including Pakistani scholars. Covers full tuition fees, living stipend, airfare, and visa costs.',
  '["# Gates Cambridge Scholarship 2027 – Fully Funded Postgraduate Scholarship","## Overview: One of the World''s Most Prestigious Academic Awards\n\nThe **Gates Cambridge Scholarship** is widely recognized as one of the most prestigious, competitive, and generous international postgraduate awards in higher education. Established in October 2000 through a historic **$210 million donation** from the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation to the **University of Cambridge**, the Trust funds approximately **80 full-cost scholarships** each year to outstanding applicants from countries outside the United Kingdom.\n\nFor the **2027/28 academic entry cycle**, citizens of **Pakistan** are fully eligible to compete under the international application round. The scholarship supports postgraduate study leading to a **PhD (full-time or eligible part-time pilot)**, **M.Litt (2-year Master of Letters)**, or a **one-year full-time postgraduate course** (such as an MPhil, LLM, MRes, or MASt) across all academic departments at Cambridge.\n\nUnlike traditional academic grants that evaluate grades alone, Gates Cambridge seeks scholars who combine exceptional academic intellect with a profound **commitment to improving the lives of others** and proven **leadership capacity**.","> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Critical Dual Application Deadlines for International / Pakistani Applicants:**\n> There is no single universal application closing date for international applicants. For 2027/28 entry, your application deadline is determined strictly by the specific **Course Funding Deadline** linked to your chosen course in the University of Cambridge Course Directory. These deadlines fall on either:\n> - **Round 1:** **8 December 2026**\n> - **Round 2:** **6 January 2027**\n> \n> Candidates must verify their exact course deadline before beginning their application.","## Scholarship Summary & Fast Facts\n\n| Parameter | Official Details |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Awarding Body** | Gates Cambridge Trust & University of Cambridge |\n| **Host Institution** | University of Cambridge, United Kingdom |\n| **Study Levels** | PhD, M.Litt, or 1-Year Full-Time Postgraduate Degree (MPhil, LLM, MRes, MASt) |\n| **Target Academic Year** | 2027/28 Academic Entry (Beginning October 2027) |\n| **Pakistani Applicant Eligibility** | Fully Eligible (Citizens of any country outside the UK) |\n| **Global Scholarship Intake** | Approximately 80 Scholars Annually (~55 for International Round) |\n| **Funding Scope** | **Fully Funded** (Tuition + Maintenance + Travel + Visa) |\n| **Living Allowance** | **~£21,000 per year** (Single student maintenance rate) |\n| **Course Funding Deadlines** | **8 December 2026** OR **6 January 2027** (Course Specific) |\n| **Application Mode** | Standard University of Cambridge Postgraduate Applicant Portal |","## Eligible Postgraduate Degree Programs\n\nThe Gates Cambridge Scholarship is tenable for postgraduate study in any subject available at the University of Cambridge, subject to course eligibility rules:\n\n### Eligible Courses:\n- **PhD (Doctor of Philosophy):** Full-time 3-year or 4-year doctoral research degrees.\n- **M.Litt (Master of Letters):** Full-time 2-year research degrees.\n- **One-Year Postgraduate Courses:** Including Master of Philosophy (MPhil), Master of Law (LLM), Master of Research (MRes), Master of Advanced Study (MASt), and Diploma in Economics.\n\n### Ineligible Courses:\nApplicants cannot apply for Gates Cambridge funding for:\n- Undergraduate degrees (BA, BA affiliated).\n- Business Doctorate (BusD).\n- Master of Business Administration (MBA) or Master of Finance (MFin).\n- Clinical medical or veterinary degrees (e.g., MBBChir).\n- Part-time degrees (outside specific pilot doctoral programs).\n- Non-degree or modular executive diplomas.","## Eligibility Requirements for Pakistani Applicants\n\nTo be considered for a Gates Cambridge Scholarship, Pakistani candidates must satisfy three foundational conditions:\n\n1. **Nationality & Citizenship:** You must be a citizen of any country outside the United Kingdom. Pakistani citizens living in Pakistan or overseas are fully eligible.\n2. **Academic Standards:** Applying to Cambridge requires top-tier academic performance. Pakistani applicants typically need a 4-year Bachelor''s degree (BS / BSc Hons / BE) or a Master''s degree (MS / MPhil) from an HEC-recognized university with a **First Class Division**, high GPA (typically 3.7+ out of 4.0), or equivalent academic distinction.\n3. **English Language Proficiency:** If shortlisted, candidates must fulfill the University of Cambridge language requirement (typically an IELTS Academic overall band of 7.5 with at least 7.0 in each element, or equivalent TOEFL iBT score).","> [!NOTE]\n> Meeting the minimum academic criteria does not guarantee admission or funding. Cambridge receives thousands of world-class applications; applicants must present a compelling research proposal and outstanding references.","## Full Financial Package & Scholarship Benefits\n\nThe Gates Cambridge Scholarship is one of the most comprehensive funding awards globally. The core financial components include:\n\n### 1. Core Mandatory Allowances:\n- **University Composition Fee:** Full payment of tuition fees at the appropriate international rate charged by the University of Cambridge.\n- **Maintenance Allowance:** A generous single student living stipend set at **~£21,000 for 12 months** (pro-rata for courses of shorter duration; doctoral students receive funding for up to 4 years).\n- **International Travel:** One single economy airfare at both the beginning and conclusion of the degree course from Pakistan to the UK.\n- **Inbound Visa & Health Surcharge:** Full reimbursement of the UK Student Visa application fee and the mandatory UK Immigration Health Surcharge (IHS).\n\n### 2. Discretionary & Additional Allowances:\nScholars may also apply for supplementary funding on a competitive or need basis:\n- **Academic Development Funding:** Between £500 and £2,000 to attend international conferences, academic seminars, and specialty courses.\n- **Family Allowance:** Financial assistance of up to £11,604 for one child and £16,548 for two or more children (single student rate remains applicable for spouses).\n- **Fieldwork Allowance:** Maintenance stipend continuity while conducting approved overseas fieldwork for PhD research.\n- **Maternity / Paternity Funding:** Interruption funding for parental leave up to 6 months.\n- **Hardship Funding:** Discretionary support for unforeseen emergencies during study.","## The Four Core Selection Criteria\n\nCommittees evaluate each applicant against four distinct selection criteria:\n\n1. **Outstanding Intellectual Ability:** Proven by transcripts, university honors, publications, academic awards, and referee assessments. Applicants must demonstrate that they have the intellectual capacity to excel in Cambridge''s demanding academic environment.\n2. **Reasons for Choice of Course:** A coherent, intellectually persuasive justification for why you have chosen this particular degree, why Cambridge is the indispensable institution for your work, and how the curriculum advances your long-term research or professional trajectory.\n3. **Commitment to Improving the Lives of Others:** A defining benchmark of the Gates Cambridge ethos. Applicants must demonstrate a tangible track record of service, volunteer work, social entrepreneurship, or research aimed at solving real-world challenges in society, health, education, environment, or governance.\n4. **Leadership Potential:** Demonstrable ability to motivate teams, navigate complex organizational challenges, influence positive change, and lead within academic, professional, or civic settings.","## Dual Course Funding Deadlines Explained\n\nPakistani applicants must be extremely diligent regarding the application schedule:\n\n- The University of Cambridge operates a unified application system where funding deadlines are tied to each individual department.\n- For international applicants applying for 2027 entry, the course deadline is either **8 December 2026** or **6 January 2027**.\n- **How to Find Your Exact Deadline:** Visit the [University of Cambridge Course Directory](https://www.postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/courses), select your degree program, and look at the date listed under **Course Funding Deadline**.\n- If your course lists **8 December 2026**, submitting on 9 December means you will not be considered for Gates Cambridge, even if general course admissions remain open.","## Step-by-Step Application Process\n\nThere is no separate application portal for the Gates Cambridge Scholarship. Applicants apply simultaneously for course admission, a college place, and funding through Cambridge''s central portal:\n\n1. **Select Your Course:** Research the University of Cambridge Course Directory and verify that your target program is eligible for Gates Cambridge funding.\n2. **Postgraduate Applicant Portal:** Create an account on the University of Cambridge Applicant Portal.\n3. **Complete Course Application:** Fill out personal history, academic transcripts, CV, sample of work (if required), and research proposal (mandatory for PhD/research courses).\n4. **Tick Funding Consideration:** In the funding section of the application, tick the box indicating that you wish to apply for the **Gates Cambridge Scholarship**.\n5. **Write the Gates Cambridge Statement:** Submit an original 500-word statement explaining why you are seeking a Gates Cambridge Scholarship and how you meet the four criteria.\n6. **Provide Gates Cambridge Reference:** In addition to your two standard academic references for course admission, provide the contact details of a third referee who will write specifically on your leadership potential and commitment to improving others'' lives.\n7. **Submit Before Deadline:** Ensure all materials, including referee submissions, are uploaded prior to the course cut-off date (8 December 2026 or 6 January 2027).","## Related International Scholarships for Pakistani Students\n\nIf you are planning your international postgraduate journey, explore other fully funded opportunities documented on CareerDost:\n\n- **Japanese Government Fellowship:** [Japan JDS Scholarship 2026 for Pakistan — Full Tuition & Living Costs](/jobs/japan-jds-scholarship-2026-pakistan)\n- **UK Government Flagship:** [Chevening Scholarship 2027–28 Pakistan Guide](/jobs/chevening-scholarship-2027-28-pakistan)\n- **Commonwealth UK Awards:** [HEC UK Commonwealth Scholarships 2027–28](/jobs/hec-uk-commonwealth-scholarships-2027-28)\n- **European Research Awards:** [Swiss Government Excellence Scholarships 2027](/jobs/swiss-government-excellence-scholarships-2027-pakistan)\n- **HEC Doctoral Fellowships:** [HEC IRSIP International Fellowship (Batch 60)](/jobs/hec-irsip-batch-60-scholarship-2026)\n- **All Active Global Awards:** Browse the [CareerDost Scholarships Category](/category/scholarships)","## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\n\n### Q1: Can Pakistani citizens apply for the Gates Cambridge Scholarship?\n**Yes.** Pakistani citizens residing in Pakistan or abroad are fully eligible to apply under the international application round for the 2027/28 academic intake.\n\n### Q2: What are the two official application deadlines for international applicants?\nThe application deadlines for international applicants are tied to their specific academic courses: either **8 December 2026** or **6 January 2027**. You must check your specific program''s Course Funding Deadline in the Cambridge Postgraduate Course Directory.\n\n### Q3: Is there a separate application portal for Gates Cambridge?\n**No.** You apply for course admission and the Gates Cambridge Scholarship simultaneously through the University of Cambridge Postgraduate Applicant Portal by completing the dedicated Gates Cambridge section.\n\n### Q4: Does the scholarship cover English language testing fees (IELTS/TOEFL)?\nNo. Applicants are responsible for their own English language examination fees. However, once selected as a Gates Cambridge Scholar, all visa costs, health surcharges, flights, tuition, and living stipends are fully covered.\n\n### Q5: What is the Gates Cambridge referee requirement?\nIn addition to two academic references required for Cambridge course admission, Gates Cambridge requires a third separate reference who comments directly on your leadership potential and dedication to improving the lives of others.\n\n### Q6: Can I apply for an undergraduate degree or an MBA under Gates Cambridge?\nNo. Undergraduate degrees (BA) and professional business master''s degrees such as the MBA or Master of Finance (MFin) are strictly ineligible for Gates Cambridge funding.","## Official Application Links & Trust Resources\n\n- **Gates Cambridge Trust Official Website:** [gatescambridge.org](https://www.gatescambridge.org)\n- **Gates Eligibility & Criteria:** [gatescambridge.org/apply/eligibility-and-criteria](https://www.gatescambridge.org/apply/eligibility-and-criteria/)\n- **Cambridge Postgraduate Applicant Portal:** [postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk](https://www.postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk)\n- **Cambridge Course Directory:** [postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/courses](https://www.postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/courses)\n\n*CareerDost is Pakistan''s leading career & scholarship guidance platform. All details regarding the Gates Cambridge Scholarship 2027 have been verified against official University of Cambridge statutes.*"]',
